  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a pathway by which Dequalinium interacts with Extracellular signal-regulated kinase (ERK). Dequalinium is directly linked to CDK3/Cyclin E, which is a target of multiple compounds, including Kutzneride 9 and 2-(5-Hydroxy-1H-Indol-3-Yl)Acetic Acid. These compounds, in turn, target ERK, indicating a potential mechanism of action through the CDK3/Cyclin E pathway. The shared target of CDK3/Cyclin E across different compounds supports the idea that Dequalinium may act through a similar mechanism, possibly by modulating the same signaling cascade. The presence of multiple distinct compounds targeting CDK3/Cyclin E, each with a unique structure, suggests that Dequalinium may exert its effects through a similar or complementary pathway, potentially involving the same downstream target ERK. This integrated evidence highlights the importance of CDK3/Cyclin E as a central node in the signaling network, with Dequalinium possibly playing a role in this network through its interaction with this target.",
